  nonce: baf7  # baf7
  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-08-09, NOT STALE -- both behaviours AND both figures reproduce\nexactly. Recorded as positive evidence because this item is 3 days older than its\nsiblings and javascript has been touched since (WI-nonad DDG wiring, PR #256), so\n'probably still true' was not good enough.\n\nBEHAVIOUR, re-run with this item's own shapes and its own positive control:\n\n  javascript  fs.createWriteStream(p)            -> 1 boundary   <- CONTROL PASSES\n              new net.Socket().write(d)          -> NO call edge, 0 boundaries\n              const s = new net.Socket(); s.write -> NO call edge, 0 boundaries\n\n  kotlin      File(p) constructor                -> emits kotlin:java.io.File:0-0:File:unresolved\n              File(p).writeText(s)      chained  -> constructor edge ONLY, method emits nothing\n              val f = File(p); f.writeText(s)    -> constructor edge ONLY, method emits nothing\n\nSo the item's exact wording still holds: 'the analyzer is reaching the expression and\ndeclining to emit for the method', in BOTH forms, in BOTH languages.\n\nFIGURES, recomputed on THIS ITEM'S OWN DENOMINATOR (write-side/sink-category\nprimitives, method-kind share):\n  kotlin      89 of 93 = 95.7%   (filed: 89 of 93 = 96%)\n  javascript  29 of 83 = 34.9%   (filed: 29 of 83 = 35%)\n  java 97.1%, scala 97.4%, swift 87.5%   (filed: 97 / 97 / 88)\nEvery number reproduces.\n\nA NEAR-MISS WORTH RECORDING. My first recomputation used ALL io_primitives rather\nthan the write-side subset and got kotlin 181/186 and javascript 51/187 -- which\nlooked like 'the catalogues doubled, the filed figures are stale'. They had not; I\nwas on the wrong denominator. I nearly filed a false staleness against a correct\nitem. Name the population before comparing to a filed number.\n\nSTILL OPEN as filed: the mechanism is read in code for kotlin and NOT confirmed for\njavascript. Unchanged."  # baf7
