  message: "P0/P1 SWEEP 2026-08-17, dev 11a240f83d. Every claim below was re-derived against the current tree, not re-read off this thread.\n\nRE-VERIFIED AT TIP, STILL OPEN, BOTH LANGUAGES. Independent fixtures at dev 11a240f83d, one run per language:\n\n    kotlin   val fh = File(p); fh.readText()\n               -> kotlin:java.io.File:0-0:File:unresolved   (constructor)\n               -> NO EDGE for readText\n    javascript  obj.write(x)\n               -> NO EDGE   (while helper(x), fs.readFileSync(x) and console.log(x) in the SAME file DO emit)\n\nThe javascript half is the more useful datum: three sibling call shapes in the same function emit and the instance-method one does not, so this is not the analyzer failing on the file.\n\nI did NOT recompute the catalogue-share figures (kotlin 95.7%, javascript 34.9%). The 2026-08-10 entry's near-miss note is the reason -- those figures are on the write-side/sink-category denominator, and a recomputation on all io_primitives reads as a false staleness. Name the population before comparing."  # 9a7f
